DM: The oasis is on this old trade road.

01:00:56.240 --> 01:00:59.900
DM: The lizard tracks seem to run east along the trade road.

01:00:59.900 --> 01:01:09.440
DM: Um, this, this man is coming not from the trade road, but from the open plains, uh, to the, to the, um, north and west-

01:01:09.440 --> 01:01:10.010
Delwath: Okay, if it-

01:01:10.010 --> 01:01:10.010
DM: ... of the oasis

01:01:10.010 --> 01:01:12.640
Delwath: ... there's nothing like, it's not like there's something...

01:01:12.640 --> 01:01:16.580
Delwath: We'd be... Is it a dir- I'm trying to figure out is the direction we'd be expecting somebody to be coming from.

01:01:19.000 --> 01:01:19.900
Delwath: Or we would have no idea.

01:01:19.900 --> 01:01:20.850
DM: Ah, you would have no idea.

01:01:20.850 --> 01:01:21.940
Delwath: Is there like-

01:01:21.940 --> 01:01:22.240
DM: We wouldn't-

01:01:22.240 --> 01:01:24.940
Delwath: There's not like another village there that we know about or...

01:01:24.940 --> 01:01:34.940
DM: No. I mean, so this, this area, in the morning light you can tell that the area around the oasis seems to be, um, greener and grassier and

01:01:34.940 --> 01:01:39.000
DM: less deserty than sort of what you were tr- I mean, it's not bare rock.

01:01:39.000 --> 01:01:43.690
DM: Like, uh, you know, two days ago you were traveling through these sort of bare canyon lands.

01:01:43.690 --> 01:01:43.740
Delwath: Right.

01:01:43.740 --> 01:01:51.060
DM: Um, this is definitely, you know, seems like, and especially going off north of the road, um, it just seems a little bit wetter.

01:01:51.060 --> 01:01:51.340
Delwath: Mm-hmm.

01:01:51.340 --> 01:01:53.120
DM: Uh, it's a little bit lower ground.

01:01:53.120 --> 01:02:00.850
DM: Um, it's definitely an area where people, you know, a lot of the D- you know, the Dunmari are largely pastoralists, right?

01:02:00.850 --> 01:02:00.880
Delwath: Right.

01:02:00.880 --> 01:02:01.720
DM: So-

01:02:01.720 --> 01:02:02.010
Delwath: So-

01:02:02.010 --> 01:02:05.220
DM: ... it would not be at all surprising that somebody might be-

01:02:05.220 --> 01:02:05.500
Delwath: Yeah, right, right,

01:02:06.600 --> 01:02:07.720
Delwath: right. Should we hail him?

01:02:07.720 --> 01:02:11.400
Kenzo: What was the name of the... Do you remember, uh, um, this, the, the la- the lady on the horse?

01:02:11.440 --> 01:02:14.040
Kenzo: She was like, "Oh, when you go to the oasis, talk to this guy."

01:02:14.040 --> 01:02:15.320
Delwath: Oh, yeah.

01:02:15.320 --> 01:02:17.020
DM: What was the name of that guy again?

01:02:17.020 --> 01:02:18.180
DM: Akan.

01:02:18.180 --> 01:02:18.620
Unknown: Akan.

01:02:19.740 --> 01:02:22.980
Kenzo: And she, and Akan was what relation to her again?

01:02:22.980 --> 01:02:24.740
DM: No relation. They just had-

01:02:24.740 --> 01:02:24.810
Unknown: Just somebody

01:02:24.810 --> 01:02:27.580
DM: ... she had just spent the night at the oasis.

01:02:27.580 --> 01:02:27.960
Unknown: Okay.

01:02:27.960 --> 01:02:30.530
Delwath: Okay. I think we should hail this guy.

01:02:30.530 --> 01:02:30.960
Unknown: Let's do it.

01:02:32.360 --> 01:02:39.520
Delwath: So I'll like, you know, go up to a, a high point, you know, or, or walk out a little bit from the tent and call out to him.

01:02:41.440 --> 01:02:42.680
DM: Cool. Uh, okay.

01:02:42.680 --> 01:02:43.540
DM: As you, um,

01:02:45.100 --> 01:02:55.400
DM: as you call out, he, he sees you and kind of pulls up his horse for a minute and, and looks around, sort of takes in the scene for a minute, and then,

01:02:55.400 --> 01:03:05.450
DM: um, starts, uh, his horse back up a tro- like, gives you a, a wave once he sees you're human and un- and s- unhurt, um, and starts, uh,

01:03:05.450 --> 01:03:07.980
DM: his horse at a trot coming down into the oasis.

01:03:11.640 --> 01:03:13.880
DM: So as he approaches, he, um,

01:03:15.300 --> 01:03:15.860
DM: he looks

01:03:17.240 --> 01:03:27.080
DM: weary and tired, and there's, um, he has a bandage around his arm, uh, and it's, it seems like, uh, he was wounded at some point recently.

01:03:27.080 --> 01:03:29.680
DM: And as he swings down off of his horse, um,

01:03:31.060 --> 01:03:35.189
DM: he's, he's limping a little bit, and he looks around at you and he says,

01:03:37.060 --> 01:03:37.930
DM: "The creatures,

01:03:39.980 --> 01:03:40.600
DM: they are gone?"

01:03:42.220 --> 01:03:43.780
Delwath: We killed three of them last night.

01:03:43.780 --> 01:03:44.680
Delwath: Were there more than that?

01:03:48.640 --> 01:03:52.510
DM: No, I do not belie- well, there was one we killed at great cost.

01:03:52.510 --> 01:04:00.740
DM: And he sort of, uh, pauses for a moment and, um, sort of tears well up in his eyes a little bit.

01:04:00.740 --> 01:04:00.770
DM: Uh,

01:04:03.040 --> 01:04:06.300
DM: uh, he says, "But no, we only ever saw four.

01:04:07.380 --> 01:04:10.780
DM: If you've killed three, then, then perhaps it is indeed safe to return."

01:04:12.360 --> 01:04:13.980
Kenzo: What's your name, traveler?

01:04:13.980 --> 01:04:17.900
DM: Uh, he si- he sighs for a moment and he says, um, "Akan.

01:04:19.140 --> 01:04:20.160
DM: My name is Akan.

01:04:21.380 --> 01:04:22.340
DM: And you?"

01:04:23.620 --> 01:04:26.180
Kenzo: Kenzo. Uh, what was the name of the, the scout lady again?

01:04:27.360 --> 01:04:28.460
DM: Alesh.

01:04:28.460 --> 01:04:29.800
Unknown: Alesh.

01:04:29.800 --> 01:04:34.540
Kenzo: Uh, Kenzo, and we met your, your, your comrade, Alesh, yesterday

01:04:35.900 --> 01:04:38.380
Kenzo: riding, riding back towards town.

01:04:38.380 --> 01:04:39.200
DM: She is safe?

01:04:40.600 --> 01:04:40.629
DM: She's safe?

01:04:40.629 --> 01:04:43.840
Delwath: She was last night, or yesterday morning.

01:04:46.120 --> 01:04:47.500
Delwath: Who knows these days-

01:04:47.500 --> 01:04:48.140
DM: He, he kind of-

01:04:48.140 --> 01:04:48.310
Delwath: ... she still is

01:04:48.310 --> 01:04:51.360
DM: ... um, like leans heavily on his horse again, and,

01:04:52.560 --> 01:04:56.000
DM: "She, she made a lucky decision.

01:04:57.480 --> 01:05:06.020
DM: It was just past lunchtime as we were resting, uh, in the hottest part of the day when these creatures came.

01:05:07.220 --> 01:05:08.020
DM: Four of them

01:05:09.439 --> 01:05:09.920
DM: running,

01:05:11.160 --> 01:05:16.380
DM: driving up a cloud of dust down the road, like nothing I'd ever seen."

01:05:16.380 --> 01:05:16.390
Delwath: Oh.

01:05:16.390 --> 01:05:17.920
DM: "Do not know why they were so,

01:05:20.140 --> 01:05:24.420
DM: so enraged, so bloodthirsty."

01:05:24.420 --> 01:05:24.910
Delwath: Hmm.

01:05:24.910 --> 01:05:26.460
DM: "We thought we could scare them off.

01:05:27.620 --> 01:05:29.400
DM: My family, there was 11 of us.

01:05:30.800 --> 01:05:32.540
DM: Only seven now remain."

01:05:34.520 --> 01:05:34.630
Delwath: Wow.

01:05:34.630 --> 01:05:37.580
DM: And he, like, pauses and takes a deep breath again, and he says, "We,

01:05:39.640 --> 01:05:44.060
DM: we fled as we could into the hills with no supplies, no water, no food.

01:05:46.400 --> 01:05:48.360
DM: So had to come...

01:05:48.360 --> 01:05:54.740
DM: But on horseback we were able to escape the, these creatures do not move so fast.

01:05:56.500 --> 01:06:01.720
DM: Those of us who are alive, anyway," he says, like, you know, voice cracking a little bit.

01:06:04.340 --> 01:06:08.520
DM: "But we had to, we cannot make it to town without, without water, without food.

01:06:10.060 --> 01:06:13.380
DM: Two-day journey through the, through the wild.

01:06:13.380 --> 01:06:17.400
DM: There's no place to get, to get water between here and Karawa.

01:06:18.840 --> 01:06:20.040
DM: So I came back to see.

01:06:21.370 --> 01:06:22.460
DM: Thank you, thank you

01:06:24.520 --> 01:06:26.640
DM: for killing those creatures. If they were still here,

01:06:28.160 --> 01:06:29.700
DM: I'm not sure what we would have done.

01:06:29.700 --> 01:06:30.100
DM: I guess

01:06:31.540 --> 01:06:33.060
DM: probably died in the desert."

01:06:35.220 --> 01:06:37.760
DM: And sort of drifts off a little bit at that point.

01:06:41.280 --> 01:06:42.560
Delwath: Are you from Kar- Karawa?

01:06:45.040 --> 01:06:45.880
DM: Uh, hmm.

01:06:48.580 --> 01:06:50.840
DM: I guess not from exactly.

01:06:50.840 --> 01:06:58.510
DM: Uh, you know, we, we have tend to go back there every year for the market and festival coming up.

01:06:58.510 --> 01:07:05.930
DM: But mostly travel in the, in the northern parts of, of this country, um, grazing our sheep and horses.

01:07:05.930 --> 01:07:06.030
DM: Um,

01:07:07.670 --> 01:07:09.890
DM: you know, the, the losses are

01:07:11.390 --> 01:07:17.850
DM: hard to reckon with right now, but sheep at least can be replaced, our horses can be replaced.

01:07:19.590 --> 01:07:19.890
Unknown: Hmm.

01:07:23.490 --> 01:07:27.840
DM: We had thought to rest a few days by the oasis with the good grazing land here,

01:07:28.870 --> 01:07:29.310
DM: and, uh,

01:07:30.930 --> 01:07:38.710
DM: make our way, uh, you know, take our leisure for a little while and make our way to town for the festival in a few weeks.

01:07:41.010 --> 01:07:42.590
DM: But it seems that was a poor choice.

01:07:43.650 --> 01:07:44.490
Unknown: Where are your comrades?

01:07:46.190 --> 01:07:48.670
DM: Hiding in the hills just north of here.

01:07:48.670 --> 01:07:51.090
DM: Did not think it was worth the risk, all of us coming in.

01:07:51.090 --> 01:07:52.350
DM: I was just scouting.

01:07:52.350 --> 01:07:55.330
DM: On a horse I'm confident I could outrun any of these creatures.

01:07:58.610 --> 01:07:59.730
Unknown: They came from the east?

01:08:00.970 --> 01:08:02.030
DM: They came from the east,

01:08:04.070 --> 01:08:04.850
DM: along the road.

01:08:08.210 --> 01:08:08.760
Unknown: Well, hopefully-

01:08:08.760 --> 01:08:08.760
Unknown: I heard

01:08:08.760 --> 01:08:09.870
Unknown: ... it's safe to bring them back.

01:08:12.110 --> 01:08:14.550
Delwath: Uh, have you, have you heard of the hyena attacks?

01:08:16.170 --> 01:08:16.690
DM: I have not.

01:08:18.190 --> 01:08:19.310
DM: Are there creatures attacking?

01:08:20.890 --> 01:08:22.180
Unknown: In Karawa.

01:08:22.180 --> 01:08:23.230
Unknown: In Karawa.

01:08:23.230 --> 01:08:24.660
Unknown: Kara- Kara-

01:08:24.660 --> 01:08:25.780
Unknown: Karawa. K- Karawa

01:08:25.780 --> 01:08:25.780
Unknown: ... Karawa.

01:08:27.450 --> 01:08:31.210
Delwath: There's been several, uh, several hyena attacks on town.

01:08:31.210 --> 01:08:33.540
Delwath: The last and, and worst, um,

01:08:35.390 --> 01:08:35.690
Unknown: uh,

01:08:36.930 --> 01:08:40.370
Delwath: unusually large creatures with of unusual ferocity.

01:08:41.690 --> 01:08:49.490
DM: As, as you're talking, he's like, it, it, it seems like he's getting over the sort of shock and surprise a little bit, and he's looking

01:08:50.550 --> 01:08:56.710
DM: a- around at all of you, and kind of takes a step back and says,

01:08:58.210 --> 01:09:00.990
DM: "Creatures of myth and legend walking in this land."

01:09:02.770 --> 01:09:03.120
DM: Is it-

01:09:03.120 --> 01:09:07.810
Delwath: Delwath just bows slightly and says, "Delwath, the elf, I'm called in these parts."

01:09:09.249 --> 01:09:10.680
DM: I had heard rumor such a thing

01:09:12.110 --> 01:09:13.620
DM: was living in Karawa.

01:09:13.620 --> 01:09:16.490
DM: I did not expect to see so myself.

01:09:17.530 --> 01:09:21.970
DM: And you, a Dunmari, traveling with these strange folk," he says, looking at Kenzo.

01:09:21.970 --> 01:09:27.240
DM: And you've all been talking in Dunmari, so he was like, took him a minute for his brain to catch up with the fact that you are,

01:09:28.510 --> 01:09:30.450
DM: you know, not what he was expecting.

01:09:30.450 --> 01:09:30.850
Unknown: Hmm.

01:09:33.930 --> 01:09:35.789
Seeker: Unusual band for an unusual time.

01:09:36.930 --> 01:09:41.210
Kenzo: Um, Kenzo kind of looks at, uh, you know, the three of you.

01:09:42.550 --> 01:09:45.750
Kenzo: Um, should we, should we take them back to town?

01:09:45.750 --> 01:09:47.490
Kenzo: Looks like this is...

01:09:47.490 --> 01:09:50.370
Kenzo: Or should we still try to work more out here?

01:09:53.090 --> 01:09:53.500
DM: Do you have-

01:09:53.500 --> 01:09:53.530
Unknown: Uh

01:09:53.530 --> 01:09:57.190
DM: ... He's looks at you as he, like, hears you s- I assume you're still speaking in Dunmari here.

01:09:57.190 --> 01:09:57.259
Unknown: Yeah.

01:09:57.259 --> 01:09:59.570
DM: As you say that, he says, "Do you have horses?"

01:10:00.650 --> 01:10:01.699
Unknown: Just one.

01:10:01.699 --> 01:10:02.670
DM: No.

01:10:02.670 --> 01:10:04.070
Unknown: Go, go get your...

01:10:04.070 --> 01:10:11.450
Delwath: I think go get your companions, and we'll at least stay here and, and make sure it stays safe until you've set out.

01:10:11.450 --> 01:10:12.770
Unknown: Yeah. All your provisions are still here.

01:10:14.310 --> 01:10:15.150
DM: That is a relief.

01:10:16.230 --> 01:10:19.430
DM: Um, and he s- as he's, he says, "I will be back shortly."

01:10:19.430 --> 01:10:22.940
DM: And he says, as he's, as he's riding off, he says, "Did you,

01:10:24.010 --> 01:10:31.590
DM: did any of you find a, a small amulet, a wooden, um, a wooden circulet?

01:10:31.590 --> 01:10:34.170
DM: It was my, it was my sister's.

01:10:35.390 --> 01:10:39.290
DM: A, a, uh, holy symbol of, of, um..."

01:10:40.850 --> 01:10:42.670
DM: Oops, sorry, where is my notes?

01:10:42.670 --> 01:10:42.670
DM: "...

01:10:44.930 --> 01:10:47.770
DM: Of Chidya, who was precious to her.

01:10:49.530 --> 01:10:50.650
DM: She lost it, uh,

01:10:51.770 --> 01:10:52.600
DM: running, and

01:10:53.750 --> 01:10:55.530
DM: if it turned up, I would be most grateful."

01:10:56.830 --> 01:10:59.030
Seeker: We haven't seen it, but we can look around.

01:10:59.030 --> 01:11:00.010
Unknown: We'll look.

01:11:00.010 --> 01:11:01.000
Unknown: We'll search for it.

01:11:01.000 --> 01:11:03.390
DM: He says, "I will be, I will be back soon," and he rides off.

01:11:06.950 --> 01:11:07.200
Unknown: Well-

01:11:07.200 --> 01:11:08.490
Unknown: A woman wearing a nice circlet, huh?

01:11:11.230 --> 01:11:15.250
Delwath: Any signs of the... I mean, in daylight, if we search again, any signs of-

01:11:15.250 --> 01:11:25.430
DM: Yeah, uh, in day- I mean, n- i- if you take some time and actually, like, look around the camp in daylight, it's, it's obvious that there's, um, you know, you find some more stuff kind

01:11:25.430 --> 01:11:33.910
DM: of scattered around. There's a, there's a small purse that was ripped open, and, um, a handful of small silver and copper coins are scattered around.

01:11:33.910 --> 01:11:34.090
DM: Um,

01:11:35.330 --> 01:11:44.190
DM: in addition to the food sort of outside, you know, scattered a little bit outside the tent, um, you know, there's somebody's, somebody's backpack, uh,

01:11:45.330 --> 01:11:48.170
DM: ripped open, and there's some traveling clothes and things strewn.

01:11:48.170 --> 01:11:58.730
DM: And you do find this, um, intricately, small, intricately carved wooden amulet that's like four s- strands braided together to form a circle, um,

01:11:58.730 --> 01:12:06.630
DM: which is the, the holy symbol of, of Chidya, who's the goddess of nature and land and animals and the seasons.

01:12:08.150 --> 01:12:11.400
DM: Um, so it seems like, you know, there was definitely...

01:12:11.400 --> 01:12:21.330
DM: The, the feeling you get from searching around is that there was, like, a panicked rush as people were jumping on their horses and running, and so there was some stuff that was, was scattered around.

01:12:21.330 --> 01:12:26.910
DM: But it's pretty easy in daylight and with some time to, like, collect it all and, um,

01:12:28.650 --> 01:12:31.870
DM: you know, put it with the food and the water that was stored in the tents.

01:12:34.110 --> 01:12:35.850
Seeker: Yeah, we can generally kind of clean up the area.

01:12:35.850 --> 01:12:36.730
Unknown: Yeah.

01:12:36.730 --> 01:12:37.250
Unknown: Maybe, um,

01:12:38.310 --> 01:12:41.170
Seeker: remove the remnants of the dissection process.

01:12:42.950 --> 01:12:43.230
Unknown: And Mar-

01:12:43.230 --> 01:12:45.150
DM: Is there anything... Go ahead.

01:12:45.150 --> 01:12:48.730
Kenzo: I was gonna say, are there, is there, are there more dwellings, like, anywhere?

01:12:48.730 --> 01:12:50.220
Unknown: Is, is, is, like, this the main camp?

01:12:50.220 --> 01:12:52.190
Kenzo: Do we see anything else kind of near us when we-

01:12:52.190 --> 01:13:02.414
DM: So again, in the daylight, you can see there were more tents, um, that were, seemed like they were destroyed- There was at least three more large tents that were destroyed

01:13:02.414 --> 01:13:03.674
DM: by the lizards.

01:13:03.674 --> 01:13:04.094
Seeker: Hmm.

01:13:04.094 --> 01:13:09.414
DM: There was probably at least six tents here, three of which remain standing, um,

01:13:11.014 --> 01:13:14.404
DM: three of which were just kind of ripped to pieces at some point.

01:13:14.404 --> 01:13:14.434
Seeker: Mm-hmm.

01:13:14.434 --> 01:13:17.454
DM: There's also a lot more dead sheep apparent in the daylight.

01:13:17.454 --> 01:13:23.374
DM: Um, some that had fled, fled, sort of started to flee north, and then seemed like they were attacked,

01:13:24.434 --> 01:13:29.964
DM: um, by a lizard that was killed, which you, you find the one dead, another dead lizard about, um,

01:13:31.774 --> 01:13:38.234
DM: you know, 200 yards to the north following the tracks where there's another large collection of dead sheep.

01:13:38.234 --> 01:13:39.014
Seeker: Mm-hmm.

01:13:39.014 --> 01:13:42.354
Kenzo: So are we at the edge of the oasis, or is this like...

01:13:42.354 --> 01:13:44.373
Kenzo: How big is the oasis, and where are we relative to it?

01:13:44.374 --> 01:13:51.314
DM: Uh, so the, the pool itself is, uh, maybe 60 feet across, like a 60-foot oval.

01:13:51.314 --> 01:14:01.794
DM: Um, it's not huge, but it's clear that there's a underground reservoir of water here, because the sort of greener grass extends maybe a quarter mile.

01:14:01.794 --> 01:14:03.974
DM: Like, you can, like, you're in a little bit of a depression.

01:14:03.974 --> 01:14:09.894
DM: There's hills that are sort of rolling hills to the north, and this area is just much greener, right?

01:14:09.894 --> 01:14:12.654
DM: There's, there's some trees in the distance you can see.

01:14:12.654 --> 01:14:15.134
DM: There's, um, there's bits of grass.

01:14:15.134 --> 01:14:17.534
DM: There's decent grazing land here.

01:14:17.534 --> 01:14:21.934
DM: There's, of course, the string of trees and plants right along the water as well.

01:14:21.934 --> 01:14:22.764
DM: Um...

01:14:22.764 --> 01:14:25.174
Seeker: I'll investigate for any geological anomalies.

01:14:27.334 --> 01:14:27.794
DM: Uh, so,

01:14:28.814 --> 01:14:30.934
DM: uh, make an intelligence check.

01:14:30.934 --> 01:14:31.934
DM: Just straight intelligence.

01:14:38.414 --> 01:14:38.794
Seeker: Solid.

01:14:43.574 --> 01:14:45.654
Unknown: Intelligent.

01:14:45.654 --> 01:14:47.454
Seeker: [laughs]

01:14:47.454 --> 01:14:47.814
DM: Yep.

01:14:53.274 --> 01:14:54.794
Wellby: I'll be right back, guys. Don't wait on me.

01:14:54.794 --> 01:14:55.654
DM: Okay.

01:14:55.654 --> 01:14:55.894
Seeker: Cool.

01:15:01.014 --> 01:15:01.274
Seeker: Huh.

01:15:02.854 --> 01:15:04.394
Seeker: So I'm kind of like

01:15:06.534 --> 01:15:11.474
Seeker: searching around, looking at the edge of the oasis, kind of like

01:15:12.874 --> 01:15:14.254
Seeker: poking at things.

01:15:16.074 --> 01:15:18.714
Seeker: Uh, and I start to go inc- grow increasingly puzzled.

01:15:19.834 --> 01:15:20.174
Seeker: Um,

01:15:21.814 --> 01:15:26.234
Seeker: it just seems like a weird place for an oasis.

01:15:27.874 --> 01:15:27.994
Seeker: [laughs]

