Seeker: [laughs]

01:30:01.982 --> 01:30:06.002
Kenzo: [laughs] I probably shouldn't have said that out loud for Tim, but...

01:30:06.002 --> 01:30:07.801
DM: Oh, I choose my words carefully.

01:30:07.801 --> 01:30:09.122
Wellby: [laughs]

01:30:09.122 --> 01:30:10.232
Seeker: He's got that look, he does.

01:30:10.232 --> 01:30:12.082
Delwath: I knew why he said that. I mean.

01:30:12.082 --> 01:30:12.362
Unknown: [laughs]

01:30:12.362 --> 01:30:13.722
Seeker: Tim's doing the face. Tim's doing the face.

01:30:13.722 --> 01:30:15.522
Seeker: [laughs]

01:30:15.522 --> 01:30:17.662
DM: Hold on. I need to look something up for Mike.

01:30:17.662 --> 01:30:19.861
Kenzo: No. You don't have to look things up.

01:30:19.861 --> 01:30:20.702
Seeker: [laughs] Oh, no.

01:30:22.222 --> 01:30:23.762
Seeker: I hate it when Tim does the face.

01:30:25.342 --> 01:30:29.262
Wellby: Let me consult the disaster table.

01:30:29.262 --> 01:30:29.272
Seeker: [laughs]

01:30:29.272 --> 01:30:29.362
Unknown: [laughs]

01:30:29.362 --> 01:30:29.742
DM: Um.

01:30:32.142 --> 01:30:33.202
Seeker: Ooh, nice oasis, Mike.

01:30:34.242 --> 01:30:36.562
Delwath: Yeah. Y- I, I switched to the oasis, like,

01:30:37.682 --> 01:30:38.882
Unknown: an hour ago. [laughs]

01:30:38.882 --> 01:30:41.722
Kenzo: Was that an hour ago? I think we were closer, like, you leaned back so now you could see, see it.

01:30:41.722 --> 01:30:45.171
Delwath: Yeah. I, I, I did lean back so you could see the water a bit more.

01:30:45.171 --> 01:30:45.202
Seeker: Yeah.

01:30:45.202 --> 01:30:52.002
Delwath: It's actually a, it's a, it's a river on the Ba- in the Bahop, and it's, it's not really an oasis, but it was the closest I could find.

01:30:53.782 --> 01:30:56.542
Kenzo: All right. Should we, uh, shall we travel east then?

01:30:56.542 --> 01:30:56.722
Wellby: Do it.

01:30:58.342 --> 01:30:59.962
Kenzo: Yes. Are there tracks to follow?

01:30:59.962 --> 01:31:00.361
Unknown: Are there lizard tracks?

01:31:00.362 --> 01:31:02.822
DM: Oh, yeah. The lizard tracks are abundantly clear.

01:31:02.822 --> 01:31:08.002
DM: Like, four giant lizards, like, running through the desert leave a trail that nobody could miss.

01:31:08.002 --> 01:31:08.332
Seeker: Mm-hmm.

01:31:08.332 --> 01:31:08.642
DM: Um.

01:31:10.782 --> 01:31:14.262
Kenzo: All right. Are, are, are any of you skilled at tracking, by the way?

01:31:14.262 --> 01:31:14.442
DM: Yeah.

01:31:16.322 --> 01:31:17.922
Unknown: Ha, the elf.

01:31:17.922 --> 01:31:18.361
Seeker: Naturally.

01:31:21.986 --> 01:31:24.655
Kenzo: I, I, you know, I just nod at, um, at Seeker and, um,

01:31:26.746 --> 01:31:28.166
Unknown: and Wellby.

01:31:28.166 --> 01:31:30.486
Kenzo: You seen an elf before the, before, before the elf?

01:31:33.506 --> 01:31:34.586
Seeker: Uh, probably not, right?

01:31:38.046 --> 01:31:38.486
Unknown: I don't think so.

01:31:38.486 --> 01:31:39.026
Wellby: Have I, Kim?

01:31:40.486 --> 01:31:46.506
DM: Uh, you probably would have at some point in your tr- your wide travels.

01:31:46.506 --> 01:31:47.806
DM: I mean, there are, um,

01:31:49.626 --> 01:31:53.376
DM: uh ...

01:31:53.376 --> 01:31:55.906
DM: Uh, but I don't think any else of you would have.

01:31:55.906 --> 01:31:56.276
DM: Um ...

01:31:59.566 --> 01:32:00.396
Seeker: I've heard tell of them.

01:32:01.616 --> 01:32:01.906
Unknown: [laughs]

01:32:01.906 --> 01:32:02.766
Seeker: Read a story or two.

01:32:04.766 --> 01:32:06.426
Wellby: I met a couple. I mean, not

01:32:07.666 --> 01:32:12.146
Wellby: ... I don't count them among my close friends, but I've met a, met a handful.

01:32:12.146 --> 01:32:12.466
Seeker: Hmm.

01:32:13.966 --> 01:32:15.466
Kenzo: So w- we, are we, are we leaving?

01:32:15.466 --> 01:32:16.346
Unknown: Are we now, like, heading east,

01:32:18.266 --> 01:32:18.946
Unknown: following the tracks?

01:32:21.046 --> 01:32:21.886
Wellby: Yeah.

01:32:21.886 --> 01:32:22.195
DM: Uh, yes.

01:32:22.195 --> 01:32:26.625
Seeker: But didn't we tell them that we were gonna stay until they came back?

01:32:26.625 --> 01:32:27.696
DM: They, they all came back.

01:32:27.696 --> 01:32:29.306
Delwath: Well, they came back. They came back and left already.

01:32:29.306 --> 01:32:29.606
DM: And left.

01:32:29.606 --> 01:32:30.946
Seeker: Oh, the whole... They all came back and then-

01:32:30.946 --> 01:32:34.146
DM: They all came back. The young guy galloped off on the horses to warn-

01:32:34.146 --> 01:32:34.596
Seeker: Everything's fine. Okay

01:32:34.596 --> 01:32:36.626
DM: ... so everybody else, like, loaded up.

01:32:36.626 --> 01:32:37.166
DM: You guys-

01:32:37.166 --> 01:32:37.446
Seeker: All right

01:32:37.446 --> 01:32:38.766
DM: ... refilled your water.

01:32:38.766 --> 01:32:38.946
DM: Um,

01:32:40.186 --> 01:32:40.206
DM: uh.

01:32:40.206 --> 01:32:42.066
Seeker: So we'll follow the tracks.

01:32:42.066 --> 01:32:50.466
DM: So the tracks, um, as you set out, the tracks, um, the tracks head along the, uh, this old trade road, right?

01:32:50.466 --> 01:32:57.776
DM: So this is a, this is an ancient road that, that cut across the country of, of Dunmar before the Great War and before the-

01:32:58.846 --> 01:32:59.806
Unknown: Ah, ancient road

01:32:59.806 --> 01:33:01.786
DM: ... the Cataclysm. Um-

01:33:01.786 --> 01:33:03.546
Kenzo: Did our old characters travel on this road, Tim?

01:33:03.546 --> 01:33:05.436
Kenzo: Have we, have we, uh, have we been on this road before?

01:33:05.436 --> 01:33:07.056
DM: Uh, yes, definitely.

01:33:07.056 --> 01:33:07.086
DM: Um-

01:33:07.086 --> 01:33:07.446
Unknown: Nice.

01:33:08.526 --> 01:33:09.946
Wellby: Oh, sweet.

01:33:11.426 --> 01:33:13.056
DM: Um, so...

01:33:13.056 --> 01:33:13.066
Unknown: Um.

01:33:13.066 --> 01:33:14.366
DM: Sorry, go ahead.

01:33:14.366 --> 01:33:18.246
Kenzo: I was gonna say, a- as we walk, can we have a conversation, just, uh, as we go?

01:33:18.246 --> 01:33:18.486
DM: Sure.

01:33:18.486 --> 01:33:18.626
Unknown: Mm-hmm.

01:33:18.626 --> 01:33:20.826
DM: Let me just do a tiny bit of description and then tell me-

01:33:20.826 --> 01:33:20.986
Unknown: Okay

01:33:20.986 --> 01:33:25.946
DM: ... what you wanna, what you wanna do as you're walking, if anybody wants to do anything in particular.

01:33:25.946 --> 01:33:27.526
DM: Um, so,

01:33:28.566 --> 01:33:28.766
DM: um,

01:33:31.086 --> 01:33:36.066
DM: east of the oasis, the road is, is hardly traveled and it's not really much of a road anymore.

01:33:36.066 --> 01:33:46.105
DM: So what, where you ca- you were following this road from when you met Alesh to the oasis, and it w- it's pretty well traveled there, so, you know, it's,

01:33:47.386 --> 01:33:53.026
DM: you know, by horses and, and herds of sheep and things, so there's a clear track through the land.

01:33:53.026 --> 01:34:03.166
DM: Here, it's clear nobody really goes east of the oasis, and so, um, you know, all you can really see besides the clear tracks of the lizards heading due east

01:34:03.166 --> 01:34:08.006
DM: is, like, the occasional bit of stone or, like, um, some bit of edging.

01:34:08.006 --> 01:34:18.006
DM: So this used to be a paved road, uh, with, like, nice edges and, like, big stone tiles and things like that, but these are mostly cracked and sort of, um, you

01:34:18.006 --> 01:34:29.006
DM: know, thrown to pieces. The area to the north is, continues to be much greener and wetter with scrub and trees, um, while the area to the south continues to be,

01:34:29.006 --> 01:34:35.366
DM: um, sort of bare rocks and heading into the sort of badlands, canyon lands.

01:34:35.366 --> 01:34:40.806
DM: Uh, as you ride along, um, in the, in the mid-morning now, I guess, um,

01:34:42.566 --> 01:34:52.566
DM: you know, the, the scene is very peaceful, if you could ignore the evidence before your eyes of these, uh, lizards

01:34:52.566 --> 01:34:54.086
DM: coming out of, out of somewhere.

01:34:54.086 --> 01:34:58.106
DM: There's flowers blooming, like, the ground is green from the winter rains.

01:34:58.106 --> 01:35:02.136
DM: This would be prime grazing land, but you don't see anybody

01:35:03.206 --> 01:35:07.825
DM: at all. Um, no clouds of dust, no nothing seems to be moving in the sun.

01:35:10.946 --> 01:35:11.355
Seeker: Is the-

01:35:11.355 --> 01:35:11.896
Unknown: So, um, um-

01:35:11.896 --> 01:35:13.486
Seeker: ... transition of the type of

01:35:14.786 --> 01:35:18.586
Seeker: landscape sharply made at the road they're on?

01:35:18.586 --> 01:35:21.105
DM: It's, it's, it's not super sharp.

01:35:21.106 --> 01:35:28.466
DM: It's, like, a few miles to the south is where it starts to transition, but the, the road does seem to be sort of the edge of the,

01:35:29.786 --> 01:35:31.706
DM: of the sort of greener area.

01:35:31.706 --> 01:35:32.006
Seeker: Hmm.

01:35:35.186 --> 01:35:39.825
Kenzo: So, um, as we're walking, you know, uh, 'cause we're all, we're walking with the horse, right, as we go, traveling.

01:35:41.426 --> 01:35:41.486
DM: Yeah.

01:35:41.486 --> 01:35:44.756
Kenzo: So, uh, I, uh, just kind of looking over at Seeker,

01:35:47.186 --> 01:35:48.526
Unknown: but, you know, loud enough... Oh, is Schwartz still there?

01:35:50.086 --> 01:35:51.306
Wellby: I think he stepped away for a minute.

01:35:52.386 --> 01:35:52.666
Unknown: Hmm.

01:35:53.866 --> 01:35:57.526
Kenzo: Okay. Well, we'll continue, and if Schwartz can't hear, you know, whatever.

01:35:57.526 --> 01:35:57.866
Wellby: Yeah.

01:35:57.866 --> 01:35:58.006
Unknown: Um,

01:35:59.546 --> 01:36:00.666
Unknown: Seeker.

01:36:00.666 --> 01:36:00.676
Seeker: Hmm.

01:36:00.676 --> 01:36:03.826
Kenzo: And I, I say this loud enough in, uh, you know, kind of your shot of the elf.

01:36:05.366 --> 01:36:05.676
Unknown: Seeker,

01:36:07.126 --> 01:36:08.026
Unknown: what do you know about dreams?

01:36:10.126 --> 01:36:11.566
Seeker: I'm very interested in dreams.

01:36:13.486 --> 01:36:14.066
Seeker: I, uh,

01:36:15.106 --> 01:36:17.486
Seeker: and I have some ideas about them.

01:36:17.486 --> 01:36:19.016
Seeker: It's something that I would like to,

01:36:20.126 --> 01:36:21.246
Seeker: to investigate.

01:36:23.326 --> 01:36:25.366
Seeker: What I'm especially curious about are

01:36:26.526 --> 01:36:30.476
Seeker: the connections between things, you might say.

01:36:30.476 --> 01:36:30.576
Unknown: Hmm.

01:36:31.706 --> 01:36:36.566
Seeker: As you've seen, I have this ability to create shapes in the world that

01:36:38.046 --> 01:36:41.846
Seeker: channel the energy around us in useful ways.

01:36:43.466 --> 01:36:49.446
Seeker: I think the way that I use this energy is a little bit different from how this elf does it or others do it.

01:36:51.086 --> 01:36:51.746
Unknown: Hmm.

01:36:51.746 --> 01:36:52.346
Seeker: There's a kind of...

01:36:53.386 --> 01:36:57.426
Seeker: Not the kind of place that we're in, but a place where that power resides.

01:36:59.546 --> 01:36:59.926
Seeker: And

01:37:01.826 --> 01:37:06.126
Seeker: many have studied it, and many tap into that energy, as do I.

01:37:08.546 --> 01:37:09.296
Seeker: I think that there's

01:37:11.586 --> 01:37:12.706
Seeker: other places, too.

01:37:15.166 --> 01:37:17.826
Seeker: This is the thing that seems less studied.

01:37:20.036 --> 01:37:20.986
Seeker: [laughs] We're not-

01:37:20.986 --> 01:37:21.726
Unknown: [laughs]

01:37:21.726 --> 01:37:26.476
Seeker: ... the road. We're just, we're getting, like, super abstract now, so we're just, like, tripping over things.

01:37:28.626 --> 01:37:30.886
Kenzo: Well, we're tracking as we're, as we're going, right, Tim?

01:37:30.886 --> 01:37:32.706
Kenzo: So we're, we're just, you know...

01:37:32.706 --> 01:37:36.185
DM: I'm just curious if anybody's, like who in particular is like paying attention.

01:37:36.186 --> 01:37:37.906
Delwath: Uh, Delwath is tracking.

01:37:37.906 --> 01:37:38.345
DM: Okay.

01:37:38.346 --> 01:37:39.866
Wellby: Wellby too.

01:37:39.866 --> 01:37:40.265
DM: Okay.

01:37:42.666 --> 01:37:45.006
Kenzo: Um, [clears throat] wait, so sorry.

01:37:45.006 --> 01:37:47.156
Kenzo: Say the last thing you just said again, uh, Eric?

01:37:47.156 --> 01:37:48.426
Seeker: That's all just to say

01:37:49.946 --> 01:37:53.306
Seeker: I have this question that I'm pursuing, which is how it all fits together.

01:37:54.446 --> 01:37:55.626
Seeker: There's this place that we're in,

01:37:57.626 --> 01:38:00.466
Seeker: there's the place that the magical energy comes from,

01:38:01.686 --> 01:38:05.806
Seeker: and then sometimes a place that you go when you're asleep.

01:38:08.506 --> 01:38:10.055
Seeker: And so my question is

01:38:11.106 --> 01:38:16.046
Seeker: where are the portals between them that connect?

01:38:16.046 --> 01:38:18.206
Seeker: Where are the intersections?

01:38:18.206 --> 01:38:22.726
Seeker: What slices run through this world that show us the boundaries between them?

01:38:23.846 --> 01:38:25.266
Unknown: Hmm.

01:38:25.266 --> 01:38:25.586
Unknown: So

01:38:26.906 --> 01:38:32.486
Kenzo: when we dream, you think we actually travel someplace, place else?

01:38:32.486 --> 01:38:34.306
Seeker: Sometimes.

01:38:34.306 --> 01:38:36.766
Seeker: Well, I can tell you about one thing that happened to me.

01:38:36.766 --> 01:38:38.846
Seeker: It was really weird, this one thing that happened to me.

01:38:40.166 --> 01:38:41.236
Seeker: Uh, my people,

01:38:42.786 --> 01:38:44.546
Seeker: when we reach the cusp of adulthood,

01:38:45.906 --> 01:38:47.546
Seeker: uh, carry out a ritual,

01:38:48.816 --> 01:38:56.906
Seeker: and that is when I gave myself the name Seeker because what happened to me on this ritual, somewhat different than what happens to most.

01:38:56.906 --> 01:39:00.446
Seeker: We travel deep down into the stone that we worship and shape.

01:39:01.686 --> 01:39:01.966
Seeker: And,

01:39:03.886 --> 01:39:07.846
Seeker: you know, my fellow classmates, my cohort, they all

01:39:09.186 --> 01:39:19.226
Seeker: saw the deep inspiration in their studies for the architectural shaping of stone that I thought I also was gonna pursue in my adulthood, just like my

01:39:19.226 --> 01:39:20.666
Seeker: parents did.

01:39:20.666 --> 01:39:23.266
Seeker: But when I got down there and went deep into it,

01:39:24.606 --> 01:39:28.206
Seeker: and deep into my own mind, I saw something somewhat different.

01:39:31.046 --> 01:39:32.246
Seeker: It was a

01:39:34.086 --> 01:39:34.526
Seeker: kind of

01:39:35.866 --> 01:39:37.946
Seeker: floating place

01:39:39.346 --> 01:39:45.386
Seeker: full of tiny points of light, which I gradually came to think might represent

01:39:46.726 --> 01:39:47.526
Seeker: other minds.

01:39:48.846 --> 01:39:49.726
Seeker: And this place,

01:39:51.266 --> 01:39:53.686
Seeker: in the way that magical energy

01:39:55.026 --> 01:40:01.046
Seeker: resides in a aboveness, even though it's not literally up above n- us, it has a kind of

01:40:02.906 --> 01:40:03.746
Seeker: belowness.

01:40:05.746 --> 01:40:08.386
Seeker: And more than that about their relation

01:40:09.566 --> 01:40:10.286
Seeker: I can't say.

01:40:11.566 --> 01:40:13.866
Seeker: But I've spent my life trying to find out.

01:40:15.326 --> 01:40:19.186
Seeker: I also, you might be interested, [clears throat] have made some diagrams.

01:40:19.186 --> 01:40:20.146
Seeker: [laughs]

01:40:20.146 --> 01:40:22.786
Unknown: [laughs]

01:40:22.786 --> 01:40:22.946
Seeker: Uh,

01:40:23.986 --> 01:40:34.026
Seeker: the lines of magic force through the landscape, the strange shape of cataclysmic changes that seem to create these unnatural geological formations, I think there's a link between them, but I don't

01:40:34.026 --> 01:40:35.546
Seeker: know what it is.

01:40:35.546 --> 01:40:36.466
Unknown: Hmm.

01:40:36.466 --> 01:40:45.696
Seeker: And the mystery cult in that town we were just in, they, as far as I have heard, have a connection to this magical dream world.

01:40:45.696 --> 01:40:53.406
Seeker: And so perhaps there's a relationship between the pattern of lines of magical energy that converge on their temple, and the fact-

01:40:54.526 --> 01:40:54.555
Unknown: Hmm

01:40:54.555 --> 01:40:59.046
Seeker: ... that they can enter into and draw power from perhaps the world of dreams.

01:40:59.046 --> 01:41:00.886
Seeker: Perhaps those things are all r- related.

01:41:02.046 --> 01:41:02.066
Unknown: Yeah.

01:41:02.066 --> 01:41:04.666
Seeker: But we didn't really get a chance to talk to them while we were there though, so who knows?

01:41:06.886 --> 01:41:08.626
Wellby: That it could be a doorway, you think?

01:41:14.046 --> 01:41:17.106
Seeker: I'd love to go through that door if one such door exists.

01:41:18.866 --> 01:41:22.486
Delwath: Have, have you heard the tales of the oasis in town?

01:41:25.926 --> 01:41:26.626
DM: No, you haven't.

01:41:28.066 --> 01:41:29.426
Seeker: Uh, nope.

01:41:29.426 --> 01:41:32.126
Seeker: [laughs] W- what are the tales of the oasis?

01:41:34.786 --> 01:41:35.526
Delwath: Hold on one second.

01:41:36.546 --> 01:41:37.506
Delwath: Let me just ...

01:41:37.506 --> 01:41:39.726
DM: Schwartz, I'll send you a message when you get a chance.

01:41:39.726 --> 01:41:41.486
Wellby: Oh, thank you. Sorry.

01:41:41.486 --> 01:41:43.916
Wellby: I'm making late night peanut butter and jellies.

01:41:43.916 --> 01:41:45.906
Wellby: [laughs]

01:41:45.906 --> 01:41:46.586
Seeker: Awesome.

01:41:46.586 --> 01:41:47.266
Delwath: There's a

01:41:49.726 --> 01:41:49.726
Delwath: ...

01:41:52.286 --> 01:41:53.146
Delwath: There's the, um,

01:41:55.186 --> 01:41:59.226
Delwath: there's a tale they tell in the village that if you spend a night

01:42:00.546 --> 01:42:09.046
Delwath: at the edge of the oasis, waiting patiently, Shakun herself will come to you in a vision and show you one true thing about your future.

01:42:12.326 --> 01:42:13.426
Seeker: Oh.

01:42:18.686 --> 01:42:19.126
Unknown: Seeker,

01:42:20.326 --> 01:42:22.066
Kenzo: the elf and I have been talking about dreams.

01:42:24.486 --> 01:42:25.126
Seeker: Have you now?

01:42:27.006 --> 01:42:28.505
Unknown: I wanna know more about these dreams.

01:42:28.506 --> 01:42:31.366
Kenzo: This is part of why I'm here in this town.

01:42:31.366 --> 01:42:36.606
Kenzo: Like you, I also am interested in this, in this, in, um, what's the name of the cult again?

01:42:36.606 --> 01:42:37.376
Unknown: The, uh ...

01:42:37.376 --> 01:42:39.226
Delwath: Shakun.

01:42:39.226 --> 01:42:40.786
Unknown: The Shakun.

01:42:40.786 --> 01:42:41.626
Seeker: Hmm.

01:42:45.046 --> 01:42:48.466
Kenzo: It's, it's strange, these dreams.

01:42:48.466 --> 01:42:51.646
Kenzo: I, I wonder if it has anything to do with what's happening here with these animals.

01:42:51.646 --> 01:42:51.766
Unknown: I

01:42:54.646 --> 01:42:57.166
Kenzo: ... The scene earlier when we first arrived into town,

01:42:58.246 --> 01:42:59.945
Kenzo: I'd been there before. I'd seen it before.

01:42:59.946 --> 01:43:00.666
Unknown: I'd dreamed it before.

01:43:02.466 --> 01:43:03.706
Seeker: Really?

01:43:03.706 --> 01:43:03.886
Unknown: Yeah.

01:43:06.786 --> 01:43:08.026
Unknown: Do you have any idea why that might be?

01:43:11.726 --> 01:43:12.706
Seeker: I wish that I did.

01:43:14.526 --> 01:43:15.366
Wellby: Wait, say that again.

01:43:17.306 --> 01:43:20.506
Wellby: When you came into town ... I, I just didn't hear what you said.

01:43:20.506 --> 01:43:26.696
Kenzo: Oh, I just said, uh, I said when I, when I came to town, the scene outside the c- of town, I'd seen it before.

